      "chunk_type": "worked_example",
      "content_markdown": "Example 4. Convert $0.\\dot{3}$, $0.\\dot{2}\\dot{4}$, and $42.34\\dot{7}\\dot{8}$ into common fractions.\n\nSolution: In the following, $0.\\dot{3}$, $0.\\dot{2}\\dot{4}$ and $42.34\\dot{7}\\dot{8}$ have been converted into common fractions.\n\nFirst $0.\\dot{3} = 0.3333...$\n$$0.\\dot{3} \\times 10 = 0.333... \\times 10 = 3.333...$$\n$$0.\\dot{3} \\times 1 = 0.333... \\times 1 = 0.333...$$\n\nsubtracting, $0.\\dot{3} \\times 10 - 0.\\dot{3} \\times 1 = 3$\n$$0.\\dot{3} \\times (10 - 1) = 3$$\n$$0.\\dot{3} \\times 9 = 3$$\n$$\\therefore 0.\\dot{3} = \\frac{3}{9} = \\frac{1}{3}$$\n\nNow $0.\\dot{2}\\dot{4} = 0.24242424...$\n$$0.\\dot{2}\\dot{4} \\times 100 = 0.242424... \\times 100 = 24.24242424...$$\n$$0.\\dot{2}\\dot{4} \\times 1 = 0.242424... \\times 1 = 0.24242424...$$\n\nsubtracting, $0.\\dot{2}\\dot{4} \\times 99 = 24$\n$$\\therefore 0.\\dot{2}\\dot{4} = \\frac{24}{99} = \\frac{8}{33}$$\n\nFinally $42.34\\dot{7}\\dot{8} = 42.34787878...$\n$$42.34\\dot{7}\\dot{8} \\times 10000 = 42.34787878... \\times 10000 = 423478.78787878...$$\n$$42.34\\dot{7}\\dot{8} \\times 100 = 42.34787878... \\times 100 = 4234.7878...$$\n\nsubtracting, $42.34\\dot{7}\\dot{8} \\times 9900 = 423478 - 4234 = 419244$\n$$\\therefore 42.34\\dot{7}\\dot{8} = \\frac{419244}{9900} = \\frac{34937}{825} = 42\\frac{287}{825}$$\n\n$\\therefore$ desired common fractions are respectively $0.\\dot{3} = \\frac{1}{3}$, $0.\\dot{2}\\dot{4} = \\frac{8}{33}$, $42.34\\dot{7}\\dot{8} = 42\\frac{287}{825}$",
      "activity_tag": null
    },
